    "narrative": "LawDog\u2019s lineup for May 10, 2026, is headlined by **Bryson Stott** (72.46) and **Taylor Ward** (70.00), who present our highest efficiency ceilings today. **Bryson Stott** benefits from a massive 18% boost due to a soft matchup against Sugano (4.73 xERA), and his ability to contribute across categories makes him an essential start. **Taylor Ward** is equally compelling, leveraging a significant 16% park factor enhancement and an favorable encounter with Severino; despite a slight platoon drag, his volume and park-adjusted projection confirm him as a cornerstone play. **Brendan Donovan** also merits attention at 65.57; his combination of a leadoff spot and a 14% platoon advantage against Martin positions him as our top table-setter for the evening.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Matt Chapman**, who fell just short of a starting spot with a 52.67 efficiency score. While **Matt Chapman** benefits from wind-aided conditions against Chandler, he was squeezed out by the deeper bench utility of our active starters who benefit from more favorable park factors or platoon splits. We remain wary of **Jung Hoo Lee** (56.98); while his leadoff role is vital, he faces an elite defensive catcher, which creates a narrow margin for error regarding his stolen base upside. Conversely, **Lawrence Butler** is a high-variance play; his 16% park boost is substantial, but he faces a tough draw against Akin, and his lower batting order position necessitates a cautious outlook for his daily production floor.",
